From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] aic8800: gate the tcp-ack lifecycle traces behind AICWFDBG

tcp_ack_init and tcp_ack_deinit print on every bring-up and teardown.
They are debug traces; move them behind AICWFDBG(LOGINFO, ...) so
aicwf_dbg_level controls them along with the rest of the driver log.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_tcp_ack.c
+++ b/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_tcp_ack.c
@@ -66,7 +66,7 @@
 	struct tcp_ack_info *ack_info;
 	struct tcp_ack_manage *ack_m = &priv->ack_m;
 
-	printk("========== tcp ack debug %s \n",__func__);
+	AICWFDBG(LOGINFO, "========== tcp ack debug %s \n",__func__);
 	memset(ack_m, 0, sizeof(struct tcp_ack_manage));
 	ack_m->priv = priv;
 	spin_lock_init(&ack_m->lock);
@@ -99,7 +99,7 @@
 	struct tcp_ack_manage *ack_m = &priv->ack_m;
 	struct msg_buf *drop_msg = NULL;
 
-	printk("%s \n",__func__);
+	AICWFDBG(LOGINFO, "%s \n",__func__);
 	atomic_set(&ack_m->enable, 0);
 
 	for (i = 0; i < TCP_ACK_NUM; i++) {
